WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.267 --> 00:00:02.535
-Thank you, Jimmy,
for having me, man.

00:00:02.535 --> 00:00:04.003
-It's so good to see you.
Come on, you got --

00:00:04.003 --> 00:00:06.272
you were kind of grooving
over there when we came in.

00:00:06.272 --> 00:00:07.740
-Yeah.
-Just a little --

00:00:07.740 --> 00:00:09.709
-Every now and then I got to
give you a funky move.

00:00:09.709 --> 00:00:11.611
You know, and The Roots,
you know, they do their thing.

00:00:11.611 --> 00:00:12.845
You know.
-God, you got to.

00:00:12.845 --> 00:00:15.481
Exactly, right. Come on.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:15.481 --> 00:00:17.350
You had some like kind of boxing
moves in there.

00:00:17.350 --> 00:00:18.618
Are you --
-Oh, yeah.

00:00:18.618 --> 00:00:20.453
Were you ever a boxer?
-Yeah, when I was young,

00:00:20.453 --> 00:00:23.088
I was a runner-up
in Golden Gloves,

00:00:23.088 --> 00:00:24.724
and I was a AAU champion.

00:00:24.724 --> 00:00:25.991
-Were you really?
-Yeah.

00:00:25.991 --> 00:00:28.160
-Wow, before a comedian
you wanted to be a boxer?

00:00:28.160 --> 00:00:29.996
-Yeah, I could do work
with these things, man.

00:00:29.996 --> 00:00:31.597
-Yeah.
-Oh, yeah.

00:00:31.597 --> 00:00:33.532
-Did you have a go-to move,
like a good knockout?

00:00:33.532 --> 00:00:35.368
-Well, you know, you got the
jab, right?

00:00:35.368 --> 00:00:37.003
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.
-Let me stand up and show you.

00:00:37.003 --> 00:00:38.604
You got the jab.
[ Cheers ]

00:00:38.604 --> 00:00:40.373
Then you got the right hand.
-Uh-huh.

00:00:40.373 --> 00:00:42.041
-And then you got the hook.
-Ooh.

00:00:42.041 --> 00:00:44.010
-All right, your hook --
you got to turn that --

00:00:44.010 --> 00:00:45.177
you know, turn with it.

00:00:45.177 --> 00:00:46.745
So, then when you put it all --

00:00:46.745 --> 00:00:48.915
when you put it all together,
you -- pow, pow, boom.

00:00:48.915 --> 00:00:50.716
-Boom.
-See that?

00:00:50.716 --> 00:00:53.052
See that?
Pow, pow, boom.

00:00:53.052 --> 00:00:55.588
-See, I almost walked out and
then you wah, wah, woom.

00:00:55.588 --> 00:00:57.590
-Bop. That's it.
-Ooh, that's when I walked away.

00:00:57.590 --> 00:00:59.392
-That's the combo. That's
the combo. One, two, three.

00:00:59.392 --> 00:01:00.760
-'Cause you fake them out?
You fake them out.

00:01:00.760 --> 00:01:02.929
You go like --- you go like,
"Hey, like, what's up?

00:01:02.929 --> 00:01:04.930
How you doing?"
[ Laughter ]

00:01:04.930 --> 00:01:06.732
And then you're, like bop,
go home.

00:01:06.732 --> 00:01:08.968
-There you go.
Hey, what's up? How you doing?

00:01:08.968 --> 00:01:10.169
-Go home.
-Go home.

00:01:10.169 --> 00:01:11.404
-Yeah, that's it. Yeah.
-There you go.

00:01:11.404 --> 00:01:13.106
-That's the way to do it.
That's the move, man.

00:01:13.106 --> 00:01:15.307
I can tell.

00:01:15.307 --> 00:01:17.476
But you stopped boxing.
Why? Why?

00:01:17.476 --> 00:01:19.779
-'Cause I got my eye swollen.

00:01:19.779 --> 00:01:22.382
[ Laughter ]
-Just a couple black eyes?

00:01:22.382 --> 00:01:24.751
-I came home and I had a big
eye, and my mother said,

00:01:24.751 --> 00:01:26.686
"That's it.
No more for you."

00:01:26.686 --> 00:01:29.289
And I've been doing comedy
ever since.

00:01:29.289 --> 00:01:30.956
-Thank goodness.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:30.956 --> 00:01:33.159
Thank goodness.

00:01:33.159 --> 00:01:35.561
You ended up moving to
New York City, right?

00:01:35.561 --> 00:01:37.030
-Mm-hmm.
-To do standup and you worked --

00:01:37.030 --> 00:01:38.931
Did you work for Sears
telemarketing?

00:01:38.931 --> 00:01:42.234
-Sears and Roebuck.
Yes, I was a T.S.R.,

00:01:42.234 --> 00:01:44.403
telephone sales representative.

00:01:44.403 --> 00:01:45.571
-How was that?

00:01:45.571 --> 00:01:47.406
-We used to sell maintenance
agreements.

00:01:47.406 --> 00:01:48.941
-Wow.
-So, when you buy new

00:01:48.941 --> 00:01:51.010
appliances, we sell warranties

00:01:51.010 --> 00:01:54.280
and stuff over the phone,
and I never sold none.

00:01:54.280 --> 00:01:55.447
[ Laughter ]

00:01:55.447 --> 00:01:56.982
-No, you never --
-No.

00:01:56.982 --> 00:01:58.684
-You just call and you go, "Hi,
are you interested in the --"

00:01:58.684 --> 00:02:00.853
-Yeah, that's exactly what
I would say --

00:02:00.853 --> 00:02:02.421
-Click.
-And they would go, click.

00:02:02.421 --> 00:02:04.356
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah, hang up.

00:02:04.356 --> 00:02:06.659
But you had some very
interesting people

00:02:06.659 --> 00:02:09.062
working in the cubicle next to
you that were also struggling.

00:02:09.062 --> 00:02:10.530
-Yes, Salt-N-Pepa.

00:02:10.530 --> 00:02:13.866
-Salt-N-Pepa was next to you
in the cubicle at Sears.

00:02:13.866 --> 00:02:16.469
-And that was cool 'cause I used
to mess with them every day,

00:02:16.469 --> 00:02:18.104
wouldn't let them get
their work done.

00:02:18.104 --> 00:02:19.772
I was always flirting
and everything.

00:02:19.772 --> 00:02:21.240
-Really?
-Yeah.

00:02:21.240 --> 00:02:23.375
-Just making them laugh and just
doing stuff and doing bits?

00:02:23.375 --> 00:02:26.212
That's wild.
I heard that they asked you

00:02:26.212 --> 00:02:28.714
to open for them for their
first giant New York gig.

00:02:28.714 --> 00:02:30.282
-Yes.
-And you did it, right?

00:02:30.282 --> 00:02:33.419
-It was a show at somewhere,
I think at the Inferno

00:02:33.419 --> 00:02:36.622
or something, and I was supposed
to open for them,

00:02:36.622 --> 00:02:38.457
and I got there early.

00:02:38.457 --> 00:02:39.659
They weren't there yet.

00:02:39.659 --> 00:02:42.294
So they put me downstairs to
wait for them,

00:02:42.294 --> 00:02:46.599
and they came and did the show,
and I didn't know,

00:02:46.599 --> 00:02:48.234
'cause I fell asleep downstairs.

00:02:48.234 --> 00:02:50.136
[ Laughter ]

00:02:50.136 --> 00:02:52.771
So when I woke up, I ran
upstairs, they were leaving.

00:02:52.771 --> 00:02:54.374
The limo was leaving.
I was like,

00:02:54.374 --> 00:02:56.776
"Oh, there goes my chance."

00:02:56.776 --> 00:02:58.677
-Wow.
That was -- really?

00:02:58.677 --> 00:03:00.079
-Yeah.
-Well, thank goodness

00:03:00.079 --> 00:03:01.814
it all turned out great 'cause
you ended up making one of

00:03:01.814 --> 00:03:03.716
the funniest TV shows
of all time, "Martin."

00:03:03.716 --> 00:03:06.018
-Oh.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:06.018 --> 00:03:08.120
-Which we love.

00:03:08.120 --> 00:03:10.489
I mean, on top of that, your
standup as well, but I mean,

00:03:10.489 --> 00:03:12.926
"Martin" -- this is just some
of the characters you did

00:03:12.926 --> 00:03:15.061
on "Martin," and I loved --

00:03:15.061 --> 00:03:17.496
-Yeah.
-There's Romey Rome,

00:03:17.496 --> 00:03:19.932
there's Sheneneh, Roscoe --
-Yeah.

00:03:19.932 --> 00:03:21.700
-Dragon Fly Jones.

00:03:21.700 --> 00:03:24.036
Are these based on real people
or just you came up with

00:03:24.036 --> 00:03:27.473
just in your head?
-I would say Sheneneh is.

00:03:27.473 --> 00:03:31.243
Sheneneh, I would say, I kind of
based off my nieces,

00:03:31.243 --> 00:03:33.179
and my sisters and stuff.

00:03:33.179 --> 00:03:34.614
Did the attitude.

00:03:34.614 --> 00:03:36.849
The, you know, "Oh, my goodness.
Oh, yeah."

00:03:36.849 --> 00:03:38.751
They don't take no stuff,
you know?

00:03:38.751 --> 00:03:40.353
"Oh, my goodness.
Get out of my face.

00:03:40.353 --> 00:03:43.056
I ain't taking no stuff.
I ain't taking no stuff."

00:03:43.056 --> 00:03:45.824
You know, that attitude.
That whole, you know.

00:03:45.824 --> 00:03:48.027
-Oh, my gosh. Did you know
it was going to take off

00:03:48.027 --> 00:03:50.429
and that you know, people would
be still talking about it now?

00:03:50.429 --> 00:03:53.065
-I wanted it to. That's why I
did all these characters.

00:03:53.065 --> 00:03:55.835
I was trying to do everything
I could to make the show work.

00:03:55.835 --> 00:03:58.003
I knew I only had one shot at it

00:03:58.003 --> 00:03:59.838
and that's what I did to try
to make it work.

00:03:59.838 --> 00:04:02.641
-'Cause so many -- you did it
and you hit it.

00:04:02.641 --> 00:04:05.077
[ Applause ]
That was the boom.

00:04:05.077 --> 00:04:06.278
That was the knockout.
-Yeah.

00:04:06.278 --> 00:04:08.247
Pow!
-Pow. Exactly, yeah.

00:04:08.247 --> 00:04:10.716
LeBron James is a big fan of
yours as well,

00:04:10.716 --> 00:04:13.152
and I think -- well, he
teamed up with Nike --

00:04:13.152 --> 00:04:14.587
was it for his birthday,
I want to say?

00:04:14.587 --> 00:04:16.188
-For my birthday.
-For your birthday?

00:04:16.188 --> 00:04:18.090
-Yes.
-They made Martin sneakers.

00:04:18.090 --> 00:04:19.659
-Yeah.
That was cool, right?

00:04:19.659 --> 00:04:21.427
-Look at this, we got them.

00:04:21.427 --> 00:04:23.429
[ Audience woos ]

00:04:23.429 --> 00:04:25.898
Questlove -- Quest,
you've never seen these?

00:04:25.898 --> 00:04:27.033
-No.

00:04:27.033 --> 00:04:29.235
-All of your catch phrases
on the back.

00:04:29.235 --> 00:04:31.136
I mean, how awesome is this?
Are you kidding me?

00:04:31.136 --> 00:04:33.439
-That's cold, man.
I was blown away, man.

00:04:33.439 --> 00:04:36.108
I was blown away.
-That is fantastic.

00:04:36.108 --> 00:04:38.777
And did you wear them?
Do you ever wear them?

00:04:38.777 --> 00:04:41.881
-Uh, yeah. I wore the size that
could fit me, obviously.

00:04:41.881 --> 00:04:44.183
These --
[ Laughter ]

00:04:44.183 --> 00:04:46.118
These must be LeBron's.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:46.118 --> 00:04:48.320
-Like for Shaq, yeah.

00:04:48.320 --> 00:04:50.456
-But, yeah, I did
wear them one time.

00:04:50.456 --> 00:04:51.891
-It's just -- how cool is that?

00:04:51.891 --> 00:04:54.827
I just love any of the people
that respect you like that,

00:04:54.827 --> 00:04:56.862
'cause I mean, to get your own
pair of Nikes from

00:04:56.862 --> 00:04:58.964
the greatest basketball
player living right now.

00:04:58.964 --> 00:05:00.533
-Yes.
-That's pretty cool right there.

00:05:00.533 --> 00:05:02.101
-Yes, it is.
-And then, I don't know if you

00:05:02.101 --> 00:05:04.870
saw this, but there was an
interview with Kendrick Lamar.

00:05:04.870 --> 00:05:06.406
-Mm-hmm.
-Who is, I think one of

00:05:06.406 --> 00:05:08.374
the best rappers out there.
-Most definitely.

00:05:08.374 --> 00:05:10.242
-And he started talking
about you.

00:05:10.242 --> 00:05:11.810
-Mm-hmm.
-And it was a really

00:05:11.810 --> 00:05:15.514
funny interview, and he starts
talking about your show,

00:05:15.514 --> 00:05:17.583
and the interviewer
doesn't recall --

00:05:17.583 --> 00:05:19.285
doesn't know your show.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:19.285 --> 00:05:20.720
And he walks out of
the interview.

00:05:20.720 --> 00:05:22.188
[ Laughter ]

00:05:22.188 --> 00:05:24.223
It's really funny, and we have
a clip of it.

00:05:24.223 --> 00:05:27.226
Could we show it?
It's Kendrick Lamar. Watch this.

00:05:27.226 --> 00:05:28.861
-I go back and watch "Martin."

00:05:28.861 --> 00:05:30.930
-Wait, what did you say?
-Watch "Martin."

00:05:30.930 --> 00:05:32.498
Episodes of "Martin."
-What's "Martin?"

00:05:32.498 --> 00:05:34.766
-And Fruity Pebbles.
-"Martin." "Martin."

00:05:34.766 --> 00:05:37.402
♪ Martin Lawrence
Martin ♪

00:05:37.402 --> 00:05:41.074
-Oh, I'm not aware, but I know
Fruity Pebbles.

00:05:41.074 --> 00:05:42.141
-Oh --

00:05:42.141 --> 00:05:43.776
-Oh [bleep].

00:05:43.776 --> 00:05:45.811
[ Laughter ]

00:05:45.811 --> 00:05:47.079
-"I know Fruity Pebbles."

00:05:47.079 --> 00:05:49.648
[ Laughter ]

00:05:49.648 --> 00:05:51.350
-Oh, that's the end --

00:05:51.350 --> 00:05:52.985
that's
the end of her career.

00:05:52.985 --> 00:05:55.221
-That's it right there, yep.
But, isn't that fun, though?

00:05:55.221 --> 00:05:56.889
You have kids coming up
to you now,

00:05:56.889 --> 00:05:58.791
like doing all your
catch phrases and --

00:05:58.791 --> 00:06:01.493
-It's cool, man. It's cool.
I love it, and I'm just glad.

00:06:01.493 --> 00:06:03.196
I'm blessed.
I'm very thankful.

